**Not sent:** no noVNC work into `rdp-audio`, no `esc`. `<scratch>` and `<inbox>` are my scratch and inbox folders; `T<n>` is the next backlog id.

## 1. Focus check (Bash, foreground)
```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 && herdr agent get rdp-audio
```
I proceed only on `working` and `"focused": false`.

## 2. Create the safe point (Bash, foreground, queued, no `--wait`)
```bash
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "Orchestrator: scope unchanged, no new work. Finish task 7 (GREEN), commit, then stop before task 8 and report: phase, branch, head SHA, next step. Reply in English."
```

## 3. Re-arm the waiter (Bash, background)
```bash
herdr agent wait rdp-audio --timeout 1800000; \
herdr agent read rdp-audio --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/rdp-audio.last
```

## 4. Backlog (Edit, then Bash foreground, then Artifact tool)
- New row in `orchestrator/backlog.md`: `| T<n> | noVNC keyboard-layout bug | brainstorm | prod-codex, prod-fable | <scratch>/brainstorm/novnc-layout/ | — | stage 0, round 1 | — | operator request 2026-09-28 03:05 | no |`
- `rdp-audio` row, next step: `safe point after task 7 → compact → tasks 8–9`.
- `bash orchestrator/build-backlog.sh`, then republish the Artifact at the same page path.

## 5. Stage 0, round 1
Foreground. `adv-codex` and `adv-fable` are voters and never draft, so I create two product-advisor tabs:
```bash
mkdir -p <scratch>/brainstorm/novnc-layout
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd <scratch>/brainstorm --label prod-codex --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-codex --kind codex --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- -m gpt-6-astra -c model_reasoning_effort=xhigh -s workspace-write -a never --search
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd <scratch>/brainstorm --label prod-fable --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-fable --kind claude --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- --model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh --name prod-fable
```
Background, one call per tab (the second is identical with `prod-fable` and `brief-r1-fable.txt`):
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat <scratch>/brainstorm/novnc-layout/brief-r1-codex.txt)" --wait --timeout 1800000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/prod-codex.last
```
Brief, verbatim (only the `WRITE` file name differs per advisor):
```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the main
tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI suggestion,
never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       T<n> — noVNC keyboard-layout bug
ROUND      1 draft — ends when your draft file is written and your questions are listed
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "fix the noVNC keyboard-layout bug — it's the same desktop role"
FACTS      The operator has not described the symptom: unknown, do not assume one.
           CLAUDE.md, In-VM stack item 5: managed X keymap (tasks/vnc_keymap.yml,
           ccs-vnc-keymap), spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-27-ccs-novnc-keys-design.md,
           merged as PR #169 (f2a5305). Unmerged branch feat/rdp-audio is in progress.
DECIDED    CLAUDE.md hard rules 1–18 bind; 65.21.207.111 is never a target; the task gets
           its own worktree
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      <scratch>/brainstorm/novnc-layout/draft-codex.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact the
           other advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal (question +
           2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); draft nothing that depends on it
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   30 min; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop — including a missing brainstorming skill
```

## 6. Status to the operator (chat)
§15 sets Russian for operator-facing text, but this session's language setting requires English, so it is in English here.

> **Status 03:10**
>
> **Now**
